`collab/1792140000000-…findings.md` and `collab/1792170000000-…findings.md`).\n+Round 2 repaired the orbit lemma (`#{[X X] [Y Z]}`) and nested tie groups\n+(`#{#{X Y} #{Z W}}`). Round 3 (this text) fixes what the second review\n+found: which local conflicts refuse (§2 D5, witness\n+`[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]`), the install-child refusal escaping decode, the\n+work bound (now an explicit budget, with body labels spelled by rank so\n+key bytes no longer grow with a stream descriptor), the A2 wording, the\n+size estimate, and the coverage regression against 6a (2-cycles and\n+3-cycles), for which §2 D6 specifies and §6 measures the repair. §8 lists\n+what an implementation deletes, rewrites and keeps in 6a. Subordinate to\n [`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md)\n (the carrier, body version 3) and\n [`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md);\n@@ -21,12 +26,17 @@ cell\") exactly. Evidence is the carrier draft §5/§6 tables, slice 6a's\n (branch `srvm-phase6a` at `d77da9f0`), and a prototype run against that\n code (§6). Nothing here is implemented.\n \n-**Recommendation in one line:** adopt discovery-order numbering now (§7,\n-option a): a function of structure, renaming- and enumeration-invariant,\n-provable by hand (§3), with work bounded and accounted before allocation\n-(§2 \"Work\"); it deletes carrier §6's refinement and search, keeps every\n-pinned root id except the one state only the search could number, and\n-refuses a precisely described class (D5) that it cannot certify.\n+**In one line:** number cursor cells in the order a canonical traversal\n+meets them (D1–D2); order the elements of a guest set or map by a key\n+that is the spelling of a speculative local run over the element (so\n+alias patterns such as `[X X]` versus `[Y Z]` are part of the key);\n+defer equal keys and re-examine them to a fixpoint (D3); at a fixpoint,\n+link tied elements that share an unnumbered cursor cell