 and\n874\t`unordered-containers-are-order-free` (`:285-304`),\n875\t`census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` (`:331-338`), the marker tests\n876\t(`:341-381`), `cursor-cell-and-identity-shaped-literal-are-distinct`\n877\t(`:384-389`), and the fixture `seven-cursor-cell-triangle-square`\n878\t(`:392-397`). Every counterexample of §6 becomes a fixture (items 12–16\n879\tbelow), including the refused ones.\n880\t\n881\t**rows_test.cljc, rewritten.**\n882\t- `refinement-search-on-symmetric-cursor-cells-is-bounded` (`:171-178`)\n883\t  → `symmetric-cursor-cells-number-by-the-component-rule`: same two\n884\t  assertions on equal roots and two numbers; the `{:search 1}`\n885\t  assertions become `{:work 1}` → `:yin.k/unsupported :resource-limit`.\n886\t- `canonical-roots-are-pinned` (`:307-328`): `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n887\t  stay; the loop plus 2-cycle block loses the `{:search 2}` assertion and\n888\t  the pin `55ff168e…`; under D6 it pins `858a891e…` with `L = cc-1`\n889\t  (and the renamed task equal); under the D5 variant it asserts the\n890\t  `:unresolved-cursor-cells` refusal with path `[15]` and cells `[A B]`.\n891\t- `intermediate-label-bytes-are-bounded` (`:400-403`) →\n892\t  `seven-cursor-cells-number-by-residue-search` (D6: root `d76d787a…`,\n893\t  11 trials, `{:search 10}` → `:resource-limit [:search]`) or, in the D5\n894\t  variant, `seven-cursor-cells-are-refused` (`:unresolved-cursor-cells`,\n895\t  cells `[a b c d e f g]`).\n896\t- `input-row-bodies-do-not-spend-label-bytes` (`:406-421`) →\n897\t  `large-literals-do-not-spend-work-beyond-their-bytes`, same body: a\n898\t  400000-element literal still emits and decodes under the default\n899\t  budget.\n900\t\n901\t## 9. Acceptance for the rewritten 6a numbering\n902\t\n903\t12. `rows-test/discovery-order-numbering`: for `fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y`,\n904\t    the review counterexample, `[x x y]`, `[x y y]`, `[#{X Y} X]`, the\n905\t    witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]` and the two frame fixtures of §6,\n906\t    `canonical-numbering` returns exactly the maps of §6.\n907\t13. `rows-test/review-counterexample-resolves-by-fixpoint`: `'a #{X Y}`,\n908\t    `'b X` numbers `X cc-1, Y cc-2`; the task renamed and with the set\n909\t    reversed gives the same root; the root is pinned `a3713a5e…`.\n910\t14. `rows-test/component-rule`: `#{X Y}`, `#{[X X] [Y Y]}`, `{X 1, Y 1}`,\n911\t    `#{#{X Y} #{Z W}}` and `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]` number without refusal;\n912\t    element reversal and renaming give equal roots; pins `07eda35d…`,\n913\t    `da69c679…`, `49d4478c…`, `18b70de6…`, `92747c0f…`.\n914\t15. `rows-test/alias-pattern-is-part-of-the-key`: `#{[X X] [Y Z]}` and\n915\t    `{X X, Y Z}` give one root for both enumerations and after renaming,\n916\t    pinned `65ba4530…` and `409548a7…`; `#{[#{X Y} #{X Y}] [#{P Q} #{R S}]}`\n917\t    numbers and is pinned `b35b8e12…`; the witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]`\n918\t    numbers `A cc-1, B cc-2`, is pinned `9600fe01…` and decodes.\n919\t16. D6: `rows-test/residue-search`: the 2-cycle, the 3-cycle, the path,\n920\t    the loop plus 2-cycle and the seven-cell state number with the pins\n921\t    of §6 (`0fe898cc…`, `0b181cd4…`, `726a9fbb…`, `858a891e…`,\n922\t    `d76d787a…`), renaming plus shuffling gives equal roots, every\n923\t    carrier decodes, and the 3-cycle under `{:search 1}` refuses\n924\t    `:yin.k/unsupported :resource-limit [:search]`.\n925\t    D5 variant instead: `rows-test/unresolved-cursor-cells-refuse`: the\n926\t    same five states refuse at `emit` with `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind\n927\t    `:unresolved-cursor-cells`, path `[15]` and the component's sorted\n928\t    cursor cells; a carrier of each built with `emit-numbered` decodes to\n929\t    `:yin.k/undecodable :unresolved-cursor-cells` with the path prefixed\n930\t    by the root, never `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; a parent whose\n931\t    install `'a` holds the 2-cycle refuses at `emit` with path\n932\t    `[12 a 15]` and its `emit-numbered` carrier decodes to the\n933\t    `:yin.k/undecodable` kind with path `[<root> 12 a 15]`.\n934\t17. `rows-test/canonical-roots-are-pinned`: `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n935\t    unchanged; `a3713a5e…`, `4993b5b1…`, `536c810b…`, `7dc3d5c4…`,\n936\t    `6ea03f9b…`, `9600fe01…` added; `55ff168e…` removed.\n937\t18. `rows-test/counterexample-search`: a seeded generator (one to six\n938\t    cursor cells over two bodies; nested `:vec`, `:set`, `:map` with\n939\t    cursor-cell keys, sets of cursor-cell pairs including `[X X]`, sets of\n940\t    sets, under keyed bindings and the result; unique elements and keys\n941\t    under decoded equality) over at least 2000 states, plus at least 200\n942\t    frame-bearing states (cursor cells in an act window, a K-frame\n943\t    window, environments matched to the free environment, and a parked\n944\t    state at a park site) and at least 100 states with install children:\n945\t    every numbered state's carrier decodes and re-emits to its root, and\n946\t    renaming every cursor cell plus shuffling every set, map and census\n947\t    gives an equal root id; refusals are counted and reported (0 under\n948\t    D6); the largest `:work` and `:search` charged are reported.\n949\t19. `rows-test/numbering-is-total`: a task whose census declares a\n950\t    cursor cell the traversal does not reach raises the totality defect\n951\t    (not a refusal) before any row is emitted.\n952\t20. `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`, `alias-topology-and-census`,\n953\t    `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`,\n954\t    `unordered-containers-are-order-free`, `child-scope-and-shared-child-dag`\n955\t    and `census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` pass unchanged; the\n956\t    rewritten tests of §8 pass.\n957\t21. `rows-test/work-is-charged-per-byte`: a state whose cursor-cell\n958\t    bodies carry a 65536-character descriptor numbers under the default\n959\t    budget with the same `:work` as under a 128-character descriptor\n960\t    (rank spelling), and `{:work 1}` refuses `:yin.k/unsupported\n961\t    :resource-limit [:work]` at `emit` and, for a valid carrier, at\n962\t    `decode`.\n963\t22. Budgets and docs: `:label-bytes` is gone (and `:search` in the D5\n964\t    variant); A1–A9 applied in the variant chosen; kondo clean;\n965\t    `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log shows\n966\t    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n967\t\n968\t## 10. Owner questions\n969\t\n970\t1. **D6 or the D5 variant?** Recommended: D6 (a search confined to one\n971\t   conflicting component, measured at 2–13 trials, 6a's roots on the\n972\t   2-cycle and 3-cycle, no structural refusal class to document). The D5\n973\t   variant is the same slice without about 25 lines, with the\n974\t   `:unresolved-cursor-cells` kind and the F4 regression (2-cycles and\n975\t   3-cycles refused) as a documented limitation that D6 can lift later\n976\t   without moving any D1–D4 id.\n977\t2. If the D5 variant: the refusal kind `:unresolved-cursor-cells` as\n978\t   proposed, or the orchestrator's `:resource-limit` (recommended\n979\t   against: it is not a budget, and carrier §10.10 says a resource\n980\t   refusal never stands in for a canonicality verdict)?\n981\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52f48666-0c9e-4ba6-9ea9-34c287559857","uuid":"290b1846-ae69-4f37-befc-8587e4bb624c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T10:56:28.246Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md","content":"**rows.cljc, deleted.**\n- `check-label-bytes!` (`:212-230`): the label-size bound; nothing grows\n  any more.\n- Inside `canonical-numbering` (`:236-355`): the label seeding\n  (`:252-255`), `ce-slot`/`ce` (`:257-284`), `positions` (`:285-325`),\n  `classes` (`:326-330`), `refine` (`:331-337`), `search` (`:338-354`),\n  and the `checked-encode`/`checked-key`/`checked-sort` wrappers\n  (`:245-251`). The `[:child (checked-encode id)]` spelling (`:273-275