`/`sorted-bytes`, `descriptors`, the census order\n(`:137-156`), `emit-slot`/`emit-node` apart from the path, `spend!`\n(`:205-209`), `emit-numbered` (`:358-363`), `emit` (`:366-372`),\n`structural?`, `literal?`, `check-abstract!`, all of `decode*` before\n`:570` and after `:575` (the order numbering → `validate-frames`,\n`:576-578`, stays), `decode`, `canonical-under`, `frame->rows`,\n`rows->frame`, `validate-frames`, and the `:bytes`, `:rows`, `:depth`,\n`:cursor-cells`, `:work` budget keys with their defaults.\n\n**rows_test.cljc, kept as fixtures and tests.** `task-node`,\n`cursor-cell-body`, `fixture` (`:16-37`), `portable-frame` and the\n`bijection` test, `row-ids-are-jing-default`, `replace-row`,\n`window-sorted-and-unique`, `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`\n(`:143-156`), `alias-topology-and-census` (`:159-168`),\n`gates-and-graph-before-hashes`, `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`\n(`:206-213`), `schema-and-literal-canonicality`,\n`child-scope-and-shared-child-dag` (`:240-249`),\n`pending-envelope-and-nil-literal-are-preserved`,\n`task-root-checks-carried-code-and-frame`, `reversed` and\n`unordered-containers-are-order-free` (`:285-304`),\n`census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` (`:331-338`), the marker tests\n(`:341-381`), `cursor-cell-and-identity-shaped-literal-are-distinct`\n(`:384-389`), and the fixture `seven-cursor-cell-triangle-square`\n(`:392-397`). Every counterexample of §6 becomes a fixture (items 12–16\nbelow), including the refused ones.\n\n**rows_test.cljc, rewritten.**\n- `refinement-search-on-symmetric-cursor-cells-is-bounded` (`:171-178`)\n  → `symmetric-cursor-cells-number-by-the-component-rule`: same two\n  assertions on equal roots and two numbers; the `{:search 1}`\n  assertions become `{:work 1}` → `:yin.k/unsupported :resource-limit`.\n- `canonical-roots-are-pinned` (`:307-328`): `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n  stay; the loop plus 2-cycle block loses the `{:search 2}` assertion and\n  the pin `55ff168e…`; under D6 it pins `858a891e…