{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfxGSf9wtg8aJ9XXqVNsn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Nothing is staged or committed; only the note is modified, plus the untracked probe and report files under `collab/`.\n\n**What the base design is.** A cursor cell is named by when a fixed pre-order walk first meets it. Guest sets and maps are turned into sorted vectors before numbering: each member is keyed by a spelling in which numbered cells appear by number and unnumbered ones by local first-occurrence index, body rank and occurrence count. Equal keys are postponed and re-keyed after the rest of the walk. A surviving tie is entered in any order only if a cheap sound test passes (complete key, members' unnumbered cells pairwise disjoint and confined to their member); otherwise the lift refuses `:unresolved-cursor-cells`, and decode translates that alone to `:yin.k/undecodable`. No components, no trials, no `:search` budget.\n\n**Deliverables**\n- `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md`, 745 lines. Rule, proof and coverage are lines 1 to 315 (15 over the 300 target). The 6a cut list with line numbers, acceptance tests, amendments and two owner questions follow. Appendix B holds round 3's D4/D5/D6 as an extension not adopted, with its proof gap and measurements.\n- `collab/numbering-probe/src/probe/discovery.clj` implements the base design exactly; the round-3 probe and log are kept as `discovery_r3.clj` and `run-r3.log`. Log in `run.log`.\n- `collab/1792220000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-revise3.report.md`, opening with the plain-language owner summary.\n\n**Measurements**\n\n| Generator | Numbered | Refused (interchangeable / not / undecided) |\n|---|---:|---|\n| random values, 2000 | 1981 | 19 (16 / 3 / 0) |\n| frame-bearing, 200 | 196 | 4 (3 / 1 / 0) |\n| with install children, 100 | 98 | 2 (1 / 0 / 1) |\n| reviewer's tie-heavy families, 1000 | 832 | 168 (92 / 17 / 59) |\n\nInvariance failures 0, decode failures 0, 6a's own tests still green. Interchangeability of refused states was decided exhaustively over every listed order when there were at most 720 orders. Host-order entry would have wrongly accepted the 21 non-interchangeable states, which justifies the test. The seven-cell triangle plus square is refused and genuinely order-dependent.\n\n**Two deviations from the brief, flagged as owner questions.** The key carries each cell's occurrence count, one integer from one pass. It numbers `#{[A B] [B C]}` and `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]` without a search and moves several fixtures onto 6a's own roots. Its measured gain is 319 states, loss 0. The `:work` default becomes 4194304 because it now charges representation bytes before every comparison encoding.\n\n**Honest size comparison.** The probe's procedure is 296 non-blank lines against 6a's 136, so not smaller in code. It is simpler in concept: one sort, one test, no search, a one-page proof with a plain termination measure.\n\n**Verdict in the report:** READY for an implementation brief, pending the two owner answers. Main risks are the unreviewed proof, refusal of 2-cycle shapes in real programs, and the byte bound refusing literals over about 30000 scalars inside guest sets."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":294960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":615},"output_tokens":796,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52f48666-0c9e-4ba6-9ea9-34c287559857","uuid":"af8a0954-3e00-4410-bef3-aa903e538a06","timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:30:50.380Z","request_id":"req_011CfxGSeRoXGDKNW3efsFKy"}
